Docker & Docker Compose: Full Command Documentation

=====================================================================
SYSTEM PREPARATION
=====================================================================

Become Root User
----------------
sudo su -

Update Package Index
-------------------
apt update -y


=====================================================================
DOCKER INSTALLATION & VERIFICATION
=====================================================================

Install Docker Engine
--------------------
apt install docker.io -y

Check Docker Version & Info
---------------------------
docker version
docker info

Start Docker Service
-------------------
sudo systemctl start docker


=====================================================================
FIX DOCKER PERMISSION ISSUES
=====================================================================

If you encounter "permission denied" errors:
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
sudo chmod 666 /var/run/docker.sock


=====================================================================
APACHE2 INSTALLATION IN A VM
=====================================================================

Install Apache2
---------------
apt install apache2 -y

Check Listening Ports
--------------------
lsof -i -P -n | grep LISTEN

Check Apache Status
------------------
systemctl status apache2


=====================================================================
DOCKER IMAGE & CONTAINER MANAGEMENT
=====================================================================

List Docker Images
-----------------
docker images

Pull Docker Images
-----------------
docker pull httpd
docker pull fedora

Inspect Images
--------------
docker inspect httpd
docker inspect ubuntu1

Run Docker Containers
--------------------
docker run -itd -p 82:80 httpd
docker run -itd --name intellipaat -p 82:80 httpd
docker run -itd fedora
docker run -itd --name web1 -p 80:80 httpd3
docker run -itd --name web-container -p 80:80 ubuntu1

List Running Containers
----------------------
docker ps
docker container ls

Enter a Running Container
------------------------
docker exec -it <container_id> /bin/bash

Commit Container as Image
------------------------
docker commit <container_id> new_image_name

Rename a Container
-----------------
docker rename <container_id> new_name

Remove Containers/Images
-----------------------
docker rm -f <container_id>
docker rmi <image_id>

View Container Logs
------------------
docker logs <container_id>

Show Container Stats
-------------------
docker stats


=====================================================================
DOCKER VOLUMES (PERSISTENT DATA)
=====================================================================

List/Create Volumes
-------------------
docker volume ls
docker volume create intellipaat-volume
docker volume create demo-vol

Use Volumes with Containers
--------------------------
docker run -itd --mount source=intellipaat-volume,target=/usr/local/apache2/htdocs -p 82:80 httpd_new
docker run -itd --mount source=demo-vol,target=/usr/local/apache2/htdocs --name web-cont -p 82:80 httpd
docker run -itd --mount source=web-volume,target=/usr/local/apache2/htdocs --name web1 -p 80:80 httpd

Inspect Volume Data (on Host)
----------------------------
cd /var/lib/docker/volumes/intellipaat-volume/_data
ls -l
cat index.html


=====================================================================
DOCKERFILE & IMAGE BUILD PROCESS
=====================================================================

Create Project Directory & Dockerfile
------------------------------------
mkdir project1
cd project1
touch Dockerfile
vi Dockerfile

Build Image from Dockerfile
--------------------------
docker build . -t httpd1
docker build . -t ubuntu1

Run Built Image
---------------
docker run -itd -p 82:80 httpd1
docker run -itd -p 82:80 ubuntu1


=====================================================================
TAGGING & PUSHING IMAGES
=====================================================================

Docker Hub Login, Tagging, and Pushing
--------------------------------------
docker login
docker image tag ubuntu1:latest yourusername/devops-aug-2024:ubuntu1
docker image push yourusername/devops-aug-2024:ubuntu1
docker image tag httpd1:latest yourusername/devops-september-2023:httpd1
docker image push yourusername/devops-september-2023:httpd1


=====================================================================
DOCKER COMPOSE INSTALLATION & USAGE
=====================================================================

Remove Old Compose (Optional)
----------------------------
sudo apt remove docker-compose

Install Latest Docker Compose
----------------------------
wget https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/download/v2.24.1/docker-compose-linux-x86_64
chmod +x docker-compose-linux-x86_64
sudo mv docker-compose-linux-x86_64 /usr/bin/docker-compose
docker-compose --version

Docker Compose Basic Usage
-------------------------
docker-compose version
vi docker-compose.yml
docker-compose up -d
docker-compose down


=====================================================================
MYSQL IN DOCKER
=====================================================================

Connect to MySQL in a Container
------------------------------
docker exec -it <mysql_container_id> /bin/bash
cd /var/lib/mysql
mysql -u wordpress -p wordpress

Example SQL commands inside MySQL:
----------------------------------
show databases;
use <database>;
show tables;
select * from <table>;


=====================================================================
COMMON FILE AND DIRECTORY OPERATIONS IN LINUX
=====================================================================

ls -l                  # List directory contents
cd <directory>         # Change directory
pwd                    # Print working directory
cat <file>             # Show file contents
vi <file>              # Edit a file
rm <file>              # Remove a file
mkdir <directory>      # Create a directory
clear                  # Clear the terminal screen


=====================================================================
OTHER USEFUL DOCKER COMMANDS
=====================================================================

docker network ls              # List all Docker networks
docker inspect <object>        # Show detailed info (image/container/network/volume)
find / -name <pattern>         # Find files on the system
df -h                         # Show disk space usage


